// [01] GENERAL
(
    posts: [
        (id: 101, board: "01", subject: "welcome to DEADLINE (read this)", date: "01/03/1997", author: "mara", body: r#"
mara:
welcome. some rules, because apparently we need them now.

1. no warez in GENERAL. that's what TRADING POST is for.
   (TRADING POST is not for that.)
2. be nice to the modem. it's older than some of you.
3. don't ask me for access 5.
4. if the board is down, the board is down. do not call my house.
5. we keep everything. that's the point of this place.

- mara, sysop
"#),
        (id: 102, board: "01", subject: "linux is not ready for desktop use", date: "04/03/1998", author: "kestrel", body: r#"
kestrel:
spent the whole weekend getting X to start. it started. i have
a gray screen and a cursor shaped like an X. victory?

mara:
you people have been saying this for four years

ghost_17:
give it another twenty

byte_witch:
it's ready for MY desktop. my desktop is a cardboard box
with a monitor on it, but still

eli:
i got sound working once. it played one beep and i cried.
"#),
        (id: 103, board: "01", subject: "who keeps dialing in at 3am", date: "05/19/1998", author: "dialtone", body: r#"
dialtone:
every night around 3am the line is busy. i'm trying to download
and it's ALWAYS busy. who is up at 3am

mara:
the board is always up at 3am. that's the whole point of a board.

ghost_17:
some of us are nocturnal

eli:
some of us have deadlines

kestrel:
i see what you did there and i hate it
"#),
        (id: 104, board: "01", subject: "Y2K is going to end us all", date: "06/02/1998", author: "crankshaft", body: r#"
crankshaft:
i'm serious. 00 rolls over and every clock thinks it's 1900.
planes. banks. VCRs. i'm stockpiling canned beans.

byte_witch:
the VCRs have been blinking 12:00 since 1985. they're fine.

crankshaft:
you'll see. you'll all see. and i'll have beans.

ghost_17:
what happens to the board in 2000

mara:
the board will be fine.

eli:
the board will outlive all of us. that's kind of the plan.
"#),
        (id: 105, board: "01", subject: "post your setup", date: "06/14/1998", author: "byte_witch", body: r#"
byte_witch:
486DX2/66, 8 megs, USR 14.4, and a chair that hates me.

eli:
P166, voodoo card, 32 megs. i have achieved godhood.

kestrel:
my brother's old 386. it has a turbo button. it does nothing.

ghost_17:
a laptop with three keys missing. guess which three.

dialtone:
Q, W and E

ghost_17:
the E is fine. i just don't use the letter "it".

mara:
the server. obviously.
